Revision history for WWW-Keycloak

{{$NEXT}}
    - The API error carries the body of the answer, cut at 500 characters
    - An answer that is not JSON is an error that names the status, the
      method and the path
    - The token endpoint is checked: an answer without an access token is
      an error that names the status, the method and the path
    - The pagination over the users stops when a page brings nothing new
    - The declared prerequisites are checked by a test that reads the
      cpanfile
    - Admin: list_all_users pages through every user (list_users stays one
      request and is documented as capped at Keycloak's default page of 100)
    - Admin: find_client, find_client_scope and find_user throw a validation
      error for an undefined or empty key instead of listing everything and
      comparing with undef
    - Diff: _bool returns undef explicitly, so it is always one value in list
      context
    - WWW::Keycloak::Auth: a login answered 2xx without an access_token (a
      proxy's HTML page) throws an API error instead of being cached as a
      token
    - Types::Standard is a declared prerequisite, so a fresh install loads
      the library
    - IO::Compress::Gzip is a declared prerequisite, so a fresh install reads
      a compressed answer in the tests

0.001     2026-10-04 18:01:17Z
    - WWW::Keycloak::Diff: compare a representation with the wanted state, without I/O
    - WWW::Keycloak::Auth: admin token by password, service account or fixed token, renewed before expiry
    - WWW::Keycloak facade with OIDC (discovery, verify_token, all grants, device flow steps) and the Admin REST API for realms, clients, client scopes, protocol mappers, users and authentication flows
    - ensure_realm, ensure_client, ensure_client_scope, ensure_protocol_mapper, ensure_user, ensure_execution_config: repeatable setup that writes only what differs
    - Live tests against a real Keycloak behind KEYCLOAK_LIVE_TEST
    - verify_token: optional typ check, keys fetched again only for an unknown key and at most once a minute
    - Role::HTTP: build_request and read_response split from send_request, error classes overridable, for Net::Async::Keycloak
    - Role::HTTP: an answer with a Content-Encoding is decoded; it used to be read as no data at all
